00:11:02,291 --> 00:11:03,125
You got this.

234
00:11:04,083 --> 00:11:04,958
[mouths]

235
00:11:06,833 --> 00:11:08,541
[Mallory] That's it.

236
00:11:08,625 --> 00:11:11,458
-[TJ] Hey. Was it good? Yeah?
-[chuckles] It was good.

237
00:11:11,541 --> 00:11:13,458
[seat hinges grinding loudly]

238
00:11:15,750 --> 00:11:17,000
Sorry.

239
00:11:34,291 --> 00:11:38,791
<i>♪ What if when he sees me</i>
<i>I like him and he knows it? ♪</i>

240
00:11:38,875 --> 00:11:45,166
<i>♪ What if he opens up a door</i>
<i>And I can't close it? ♪</i>

241
00:11:45,250 --> 00:11:46,833
[sniffles]

242
00:11:46,916 --> 00:11:50,583
<i>♪ What happens then? ♪</i>

243
00:11:50,666 --> 00:11:53,916
<i>♪ If when he holds me ♪</i>

244
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:56,291
<i>♪ My heart is set in motion ♪</i>

245
00:11:56,375 --> 00:11:57,958
<i>♪ I'm not prepared for that ♪</i>

246
00:11:58,041 --> 00:12:02,666
<i>♪I'm scared of breaking open ♪</i>

247
00:12:04,166 --> 00:12:09,250
<i>♪ But still I can't help from hoping ♪</i>

248
00:12:12,250 --> 00:12:18,541
<i>♪ To find someone to talk to ♪</i>

249
00:12:19,500 --> 00:12:25,333
<i>♪ Who likes the way I am ♪</i>

250
00:12:26,208 --> 00:12:31,000
<i>♪ Someone who, when he sees me ♪</i>

251
00:12:31,083 --> 00:12:32,791
[breathing shakily]

252
00:12:32,875 --> 00:12:39,208
<i>♪ Wants to again ♪</i>

253
00:12:42,833 --> 00:12:44,000
[applause]

254
00:12:53,750 --> 00:12:54,708
Hi!

255
00:12:54,791 --> 00:12:57,166
-[Ted] How'd the audition go?
-[brother] I want him not to run!

256
00:12:57,250 --> 00:12:58,958
-[Sophie] It was fine.
-My turn! Me first!

257
00:12:59,041 --> 00:13:00,750
-[Sophie] Get off. Stop.
-Boys, boys, boys.

258
00:13:00,833 --> 00:13:03,541
-[Elizabeth] Boys, be gentle.
-[Ted] Hey. I got ya. I got ya.

259
00:13:03,625 --> 00:13:06,458
There must be more to the story
than "fine," right?

260
00:13:07,166 --> 00:13:08,083
I don't know.

261
00:13:08,583 --> 00:13:11,250
[Ted] Hey, guys, uh… why don't we
go to the living room for a minute?

262
00:13:11,333 --> 00:13:13,375
Mom and I need
to talk to you about something.

263
00:13:13,875 --> 00:13:14,875
Come on, Soph.

264
00:13:20,666 --> 00:13:23,375
-["A Good Thing" by Claud playing]
-[phone ringing]

265
00:13:24,833 --> 00:13:26,791
<i>♪ Don't try and fix it if-- ♪</i>

266
00:13:26,875 --> 00:13:28,791
-[turns music off]
-[phone chimes]

267
00:13:29,666 --> 00:13:31,083
It came back.

268
00:13:32,375 --> 00:13:33,208
[Carolyn] <i>No.</i>

269
00:13:33,708 --> 00:13:35,750
Yeah. They said she's gonna fight it.

270
00:13:36,750 --> 00:13:38,666
To figure out a treatment plan, but…

271
00:13:38,750 --> 00:13:42,125
Right. And they figured it out
last time, so…

272
00:13:43,583 --> 00:13:45,541
I don't want anyone to know.

273
00:13:45,625 --> 00:13:47,166
<i>I totally get that.</i>

274
00:13:48,500 --> 00:13:50,291
I'm here for you. Okay?

275
00:13:51,166 --> 00:13:52,458
Always.

276
00:13:54,833 --> 00:13:57,166
They didn't even tell me
they were going in today.

277
00:13:57,666 --> 00:13:59,416
She didn't even seem like she…

278
00:14:01,875 --> 00:14:03,125
I'm gonna go.

279
00:14:03,666 --> 00:14:05,166
-Soph…
-[disconnection tone beeps]

280
00:14:10,166 --> 00:14:11,583
[sobbing]

281
00:14:11,666 --> 00:14:13,666
[poignant music playing]

282
00:14:44,833 --> 00:14:46,000
[Trista] <i>The cast list is out!</i>

283
00:14:46,666 --> 00:14:50,500
Attention all thespians,
the cast list is out!

284
00:14:51,083 --> 00:14:52,375
-Sorry!
-[girl 1] Trista!

285
00:14:52,916 --> 00:14:54,125
Are you ready?

286
00:14:54,791 --> 00:14:58,083
-Mmm… I don't know.
-[lockers open and slam]

287
00:14:58,166 --> 00:15:01,375
-You don't have to do it, you know.
-Uh, what?

288
00:15:01,458 --> 00:15:03,625
I'm not trying to be rude.
It's just, you're a sophomore.

289
00:15:03,708 --> 00:15:06,916
I mean… have you ever even done
a summer intensive?

290
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:09,208
Wait, I'm so confused. Did I get Dawn?

291
00:15:09,291 --> 00:15:10,541
I'm gonna get in there.

292
00:15:12,208 --> 00:15:13,250
I got Dawn.

293
00:15:14,208 --> 00:15:15,291
Mal… Mal, let's just…

294
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:18,250
[Carolyn] Um… Sophie?

295
00:15:19,083 --> 00:15:20,500
[exciting music playing]

296
00:15:20,583 --> 00:15:21,750
[girl 2] Here she is.

297
00:15:29,791 --> 00:15:31,000
[Ted] Guys, there you go.

298
00:15:31,083 --> 00:15:32,375
[entry bell jangles]

299
00:15:32,458 --> 00:15:33,541
I got the lead.

300
00:15:34,208 --> 00:15:35,583
Oh, hey. What's up?

301
00:15:36,166 --> 00:15:37,500
I got the lead.

302
00:15:39,041 --> 00:15:40,458
Annie? You got Annie?

303
00:15:40,541 --> 00:15:41,916
-[Ted] What do you mean, Annie?
-Yeah.

304
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:44,375
-No, she got the… the lead. Jenna.
-You got the <i>lead </i>lead?

305
00:15:44,458 --> 00:15:45,583
The… the lead, the Annie?

306
00:15:45,666 --> 00:15:47,166
-Yes.
-Whoa!

307
00:15:47,250 --> 00:15:49,333
-[Ted] Congratulations.
-[Lenny] Mazel tov, Sophie.

308
00:15:49,416 --> 00:15:52,166
-[Elizabeth] Ooh!
-[Ted] My baby got the lead in the play!

309
00:15:52,250 --> 00:15:55,125
-Oh, we have to go eat and celebrate.
-[Ted] Yeah, yeah. We'll go out.

310
00:15:55,208 --> 00:15:58,875
<i>♪ The sun'll come out tomorrow ♪</i>

311
00:15:58,958 --> 00:16:02,833
<i>-♪ Bet your bottom dollar that tomorrow ♪</i>
-[Ted joins in] <i>♪Tomorrow ♪</i>

312
00:16:02,916 --> 00:16:05,500
<i>♪ There'll be sun ♪</i>

313
00:16:05,583 --> 00:16:08,083
<i>♪ Tomorrow, tomorr-- ♪</i>

314
00:16:08,166 --> 00:16:10,083
Musicals are stupid.

315
00:16:10,166 --> 00:16:11,750
Oh, come on, buddy. Don't say stupid.

316
00:16:11,833 --> 00:16:13,666
Why do they sing? Just be talking.

317
00:16:13,750 --> 00:16:17,458
Because music can make you feel things
that are bigger than just talking, Caleb.

318
00:16:17,541 --> 00:16:22,375
It shows people going through stuff,
like when things are hard or fun.

319
00:16:22,458 --> 00:16:24,375
You can see how
other people go through that too.

320
00:16:24,458 --> 00:16:25,916
What's the stuff in your one?

321
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:29,333
Well, I play Jenna,
who is pregnant and bakes pies.

322
00:16:29,416 --> 00:16:31,083
And her husband…

323
00:16:31,166 --> 00:16:34,541
isn't nice like Dad, and then
she falls in love with her gynecologist.

324
00:16:34,625 --> 00:16:36,208
-Her what?
-[Ted] Wait, hold on.

325
00:16:36,291 --> 00:16:37,958
Wasn't last year, like, fairy tales?

326
00:16:38,541 --> 00:16:40,541
-It was Sondheim.
-[woman] Elizabeth.

327
00:16:41,166 --> 00:16:42,083
Hi, Shelly.

328
00:16:42,791 --> 00:16:44,166
I just heard.

329
00:16:44,250 --> 00:16:45,375
I'm so sorry.

330
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:47,041
Um…

331
00:16:47,125 --> 00:16:51,416
We are actually celebrating Sophie
tonight. She got the lead in her play.

332
00:16:51,500 --> 00:16:54,333
And you brought her to Lee's.
You're such a good mom.

333
00:16:54,416 --> 00:16:56,250
You're gonna beat it just like last time.

334
00:16:56,333 --> 00:17:00,500
I said to June Nizio,
"I can't believe out of everyone…"

335
00:17:00,583 --> 00:17:02,250
[Sophie] <i>Mom, maybe</i>
<i>I shouldn't do the show.</i>

336
00:17:02,333 --> 00:17:04,291
-[Elizabeth] Of course you should.
-[boys barking]

337
00:17:04,375 --> 00:17:07,125
[Elizabeth] I love watching you perform.

338
00:17:07,208 --> 00:17:10,541
I will never forget your first solo.

339
00:17:10,625 --> 00:17:12,458
-The second-grade concert.
-[Ted] The back seat.

340
00:17:12,541 --> 00:17:18,000
<i>-♪ You just gotta ignite the light ♪</i>
-Oh, please don't do this.

341
00:17:18,083 --> 00:17:22,041
<i>-♪ And let it shine ♪</i>
-[Sophie laughs]

342
00:17:22,125 --> 00:17:24,916
<i>-♪ Just own the night ♪</i>
-[Sophie] Mom!

343
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:28,000
-Stop!
<i>-♪ Like the 4th of July ♪</i>

344
00:17:28,083 --> 00:17:29,208
Okay, enough.

345
00:17:29,291 --> 00:17:32,791
<i>♪ 'Cause baby, you're a fire… ♪ </i>[chuckles]

346
00:17:32,875 --> 00:17:35,500
-You were so good, though.
-Thank you.

347
00:17:35,583 --> 00:17:37,875
-I cried so much. Oh.
-[gentle music playing]

348
00:17:38,375 --> 00:17:39,541
Get ready to weep.

349
00:17:39,625 --> 00:17:42,208
Okay, I'm gonna put it in the calendar.

350
00:17:42,958 --> 00:17:45,291
What are the exact dates?

351
00:17:45,375 --> 00:17:48,250
-Uh, May 15th and 16th.
-Okay.

352
00:17:48,791 --> 00:17:49,833
15th… Oh.

353
00:17:51,541 --> 00:17:53,958
It's just a couple of weeks
before the beach rental.

354
00:17:54,041 --> 00:17:55,583
This is gonna be great.

355
00:17:56,291 --> 00:17:57,708
We're still going?

356
00:17:59,416 --> 00:18:00,958
To the Crane House?

357
00:18:01,958 --> 00:18:04,500
Honey, yeah.
Of course we're going to the beach.

358
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:06,583
-We always go to the beach.
-[car starts]

359
00:18:06,666 --> 00:18:08,958
[boys barking and growling]

360
00:18:10,833 --> 00:18:13,125
[Ted] Please get in.
They've been doing this the whole time.

361
00:18:13,208 --> 00:18:15,166
-[Elizabeth] I'm sorry.
-What are you doing out here?

362
00:18:15,250 --> 00:18:16,500
-[Elizabeth] Talking.
-[Sophie] Yeah.

363
00:18:16,583 --> 00:18:18,583
-[pop music playing]
-[girl] Yeah, sounds nice.

364
00:18:19,416 --> 00:18:21,041
[laughter]

365
00:18:29,041 --> 00:18:30,416
[boy] Nice highlighting.

366
00:18:30,500 --> 00:18:32,375
[Sophie] Oh, um… it's just normal.

367
00:18:32,458 --> 00:18:34,833
-Here. You can have it.
-But you're not done.

368
00:18:34,916 --> 00:18:39,791
Uh… No, I like to take highlighter breaks
so I don't get carpal tunnel syndrome.

369
00:18:39,875 --> 00:18:42,958
Have you heard of carpal tunnel?
It… it affects your ligaments.

370
00:18:43,041 --> 00:18:44,125
Sophie, right?

371
00:18:44,208 --> 00:18:46,791
Uh, that is indeed my name.

372
00:18:46,875 --> 00:18:48,958
I'm Jack. I'm playing Dr. Pomatter.

373
00:18:49,041 --> 00:18:51,916
Yeah. We're gonna do
a lot of fun stuff together

374
00:18:52,416 --> 00:18:53,500
onstage.

375
00:18:59,166 --> 00:19:00,333
Oh.

376
00:19:00,416 --> 00:19:01,500
[door opens]

377
00:19:01,583 --> 00:19:02,916
[Ms. Parker] Hello, thespians!

378
00:19:03,500 --> 00:19:04,833
Let's rehearse.

379
00:19:08,750 --> 00:19:10,666
Can you feel my hand and how sweaty it is?

380
00:19:10,750 --> 00:19:12,000
Yeah. Hmm.

381
00:19:12,083 --> 00:19:15,541
It's slimy, it's clammy, it's oddly hot.

382
00:19:15,625 --> 00:19:18,708
-All the things you don't want it to be.
-Aw, thank you.

383
00:19:18,791 --> 00:19:20,500
One, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight.

384
00:19:20,583 --> 00:19:23,291
[group repeating] One, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight.

385
00:19:23,375 --> 00:19:25,458
One, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight.

386
00:19:25,541 --> 00:19:28,291
One, two, three, four, five, six, seven!

387
00:19:28,375 --> 00:19:31,041
One, two, three, four.
One, two, three, four.

388
00:19:31,125 --> 00:19:33,083
One, two, three. One, two, three.

389
00:19:33,166 --> 00:19:34,708
One, two. One, two. One, two, one.

390
00:19:34,791 --> 00:19:36,666
One! One! One! One! One!

391
00:19:36,750 --> 00:19:40,833
[all shout, one at a time] Wah! Wah! Wah!
Wah! Wah! Wah! Wah! Wah! Wah! Wah! Wah!

392
00:19:40,916 --> 00:19:42,250
[clapping]

393
00:19:42,333 --> 00:19:44,375
[chanting rhythmically]

394
00:19:44,458 --> 00:19:45,791
-[girl 1] Cherry!
-[Sophie] Oi!

395
00:19:45,875 --> 00:19:47,458
-[girl 1] Bufala!
-[Sophie] Cherry!

396
00:19:47,541 --> 00:19:48,750
-[girl 1] Orange.
-[Mallory] Oi!

397
00:19:48,833 --> 00:19:50,208
-[girl 1] Bufala.
-[Mallory] Apple.

398
00:19:50,291 --> 00:19:51,458
-[girl 1] Apple.
-[boy 1] Oi!

399
00:19:51,541 --> 00:19:52,916
-[girl 1] Bufala.
-[Sophie] Pineapple.

400
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:54,041
-[girl 1] Pineapple.
-[Mr. Stewart] Oi!

401
00:19:54,125 --> 00:19:54,958
[girl 1] Bufala.

402
00:19:55,041 --> 00:19:59,333
-Passion fruit! Passion fruit!
-[all] Oi, oi, oi! Oh!

403
00:20:01,083 --> 00:20:02,666
Hi, I'm Dr. Pomatter.

404
00:20:02,750 --> 00:20:06,125
I just moved here from Connecticut,
and I'm a gynecologist.

405
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:10,125
[Southern accent] Hi, my name's Jebba…
I… I mean, Jenna.

406
00:20:10,208 --> 00:20:13,875
-And, um, my baby's got a belly in it.
-[group giggling and whispering]

407
00:20:13,958 --> 00:20:15,250
[Southern accent] My name's Dawn,

408
00:20:15,333 --> 00:20:17,666
and my baby certainly
does not have a belly in it!

409
00:20:17,750 --> 00:20:18,625
[laughter]

410
00:20:18,708 --> 00:20:21,000
And my heart belongs
to the History Channel.

411
00:20:21,083 --> 00:20:21,958
-Mm-hmm.
-Oh!

412
00:20:22,041 --> 00:20:27,166
[exaggeratedly] I'm old Joe, the diner
owner, and my body's deterioratin'.

413
00:20:27,250 --> 00:20:28,250
[laughter]

414
00:20:28,333 --> 00:20:31,875
I play ensemble-slash-pie shop
customer number three,

415
00:20:31,958 --> 00:20:35,083
and you don't want to go in my basement.

416
00:20:35,166 --> 00:20:36,500
-[giggles]
-Huh?

417
00:20:39,291 --> 00:20:40,583
[keys jangle]

418
00:20:40,666 --> 00:20:43,208
Who's ready for a driving lesson?

419
00:20:44,125 --> 00:20:46,041
Oh, no! What's wrong?

420
00:20:50,333 --> 00:20:52,666
-Okay. No driving lesson?
-[door slams]

421
00:20:53,375 --> 00:20:55,375
[car door alarm pinging]

422
00:20:57,833 --> 00:20:58,750
What happened?

423
00:20:58,833 --> 00:21:02,291
Everyone's accent sounds so good,
and I sound…

424
00:21:02,375 --> 00:21:04,416
ugh, like a cartoon rooster.

425
00:21:05,416 --> 00:21:07,291
Mom, it's not funny.

426
00:21:07,916 --> 00:21:08,750
Sorry.

427
00:21:09,875 --> 00:21:11,916
Maybe Ms. Parker made a mistake.

428
00:21:15,083 --> 00:21:16,125
You know what?

429
00:21:17,666 --> 00:21:19,166
I think I have an idea.

430
00:21:19,250 --> 00:21:21,291
[starts engine]

431
00:21:22,833 --> 00:21:24,833
-Mom, where are we even going?
-Hmm… Mmm!

432
00:21:25,458 --> 00:21:26,416
[clears throat]

433
00:21:29,750 --> 00:21:32,833
[Southern accent] Uh, excuse me, Angel.

434
00:21:32,916 --> 00:21:36,583
Ahem. My daughter and I
are visitin' from Georgia,

435
00:21:36,666 --> 00:21:40,416
and we're lookin' to buy
some bathin' suits.

436
00:21:41,125 --> 00:21:44,250
Why don't you tell the nice lady
what kind of suit you want?

437
00:21:44,333 --> 00:21:46,041
No, it's… it's fine.

438
00:21:46,708 --> 00:21:50,708
Go ahead.
Tell her what kind of suit you fancy.

439
00:21:50,791 --> 00:21:52,500
Um…

440
00:21:52,583 --> 00:21:55,041
[Southern accent] Somethin', uh… sparkly.

441
00:21:55,125 --> 00:21:56,375
Sparkly.

442
00:21:57,458 --> 00:21:58,500
And what else?

443
00:21:59,833 --> 00:22:01,125
With ruffles.

444
00:22:01,208 --> 00:22:02,583
-Ruffles.
-Mm-hmm.

445
00:22:03,250 --> 00:22:04,541
We don't really have that.

446
00:22:04,625 --> 00:22:05,916
Well, y'all should.

447
00:22:06,000 --> 00:22:10,583
My daughter is Miss Savannah,
and y'all just lost her business.

448
00:22:14,250 --> 00:22:16,500
-Bless your heart.
-[giggles]

449
00:22:16,583 --> 00:22:18,833
["Tiny Moves" by Bleachers playing]

450
00:22:20,875 --> 00:22:22,875
-[Elizabeth] Ooh.
-[Sophie] Oh.

451
00:22:23,416 --> 00:22:27,125
This chair is just much too firm
for my lil' bottom.

452
00:22:27,208 --> 00:22:30,458
And this one's just too tiny
for my big 'un.

453
00:22:30,541 --> 00:22:33,541
-[normally] Honey, you have the best butt.
-Mom, don't do that.

454
00:22:36,833 --> 00:22:37,750
[Southern accent] Oh!

455
00:22:39,000 --> 00:22:40,416
It spins!

456
00:22:40,500 --> 00:22:41,958
Fancy!

457
00:22:42,041 --> 00:22:43,416
-[chairs rumbling]
-[both giggling]

458
00:22:43,500 --> 00:22:44,833
<i>♪ Whoa, oh, oh! ♪</i>

459
00:22:45,666 --> 00:22:47,666
<i>♪ Watchin' it all come down ♪</i>

460
00:22:48,708 --> 00:22:51,000
<i>♪ Watch it go round and round… ♪</i>

461
00:22:51,083 --> 00:22:55,000
[Southern accent] I'll have ten
of your finest buttermilk biscuits

462
00:22:55,083 --> 00:22:56,791
and a gallon of sweet tea.

463
00:22:59,041 --> 00:23:00,458
This is a pizza place.

464
00:23:00,541 --> 00:23:02,958
<i>♪ On the edge again, on the edge again… ♪</i>

465
00:23:03,041 --> 00:23:05,000
-[Elizabeth laughing] Oh!
-[Sophie] Hey!

466
00:23:05,083 --> 00:23:07,000
[Elizabeth] <i>"Now remember what I said."</i>

467
00:23:07,083 --> 00:23:10,000
"Don't you go lovin' that baby
more than me."

468
00:23:10,541 --> 00:23:15,083
"I don't love you anymore, Earl.
I haven't in a very long time."

469
00:23:18,541 --> 00:23:19,708
What?

470
00:23:21,125 --> 00:23:23,750
Ms. Parker didn't make a mistake.

471
00:23:30,208 --> 00:23:31,500
[sighs]

472
00:23:31,583 --> 00:23:33,958
Ahem. "That's not funny, Jenna."

473
00:23:34,041 --> 00:23:35,833
[Sophie] <i>♪ She is messy ♪</i>

474
00:23:36,500 --> 00:23:39,041
<i>-♪ But she's kind ♪</i>
-[mouthing]

475
00:23:39,125 --> 00:23:44,583
<i>♪ She is lonely most of the time ♪</i>

476
00:23:44,666 --> 00:23:46,750
-Okay, uh, let's pause.
-[piano stops]

477
00:23:47,458 --> 00:23:48,791
-[sighs]
-[Ms. Parker] Um…

478
00:23:49,791 --> 00:23:51,250
What are you feeling right now?

479
00:23:51,333 --> 00:23:54,375
Uh, like I need a lot more practice.

480
00:23:54,458 --> 00:23:56,875
Well, that's Sophie. You're Jenna.

481
00:23:58,416 --> 00:23:59,500
Jenna,

482
00:24:00,250 --> 00:24:04,333
everything in her life
has built to this moment right now.

483
00:24:04,416 --> 00:24:06,708
Yeah, I know. I just…
I really want to get the notes right.

484
00:24:07,291 --> 00:24:09,291
Forget about the notes, all right?

485
00:24:11,375 --> 00:24:14,000
I want you to mess up.

486
00:24:14,791 --> 00:24:16,500
That's how you get to the good stuff.

487
00:24:17,000 --> 00:24:19,000
There's so much going on
in your life right now.

488
00:24:19,083 --> 00:24:22,500
-What are you talking about?
-You're gonna have a baby, Jenna.

489
00:24:24,000 --> 00:24:25,125
Right.

490
00:24:26,208 --> 00:24:28,625
[Ms. Parker] Right. So put it in the song.

491
00:24:28,708 --> 00:24:29,833
-Hmm?
-Right.

492
00:24:29,916 --> 00:24:31,750
[Ms. Parker] Um, let's take it from…

493
00:24:31,833 --> 00:24:34,583
["Eventually" by Tame Impala
playing on speakers]

494
00:24:34,666 --> 00:24:36,166
[Carolyn] Another thing about Erin…

495
00:24:39,291 --> 00:24:40,375
You okay?

496
00:24:41,000 --> 00:24:41,833
Yeah.

497
00:24:41,916 --> 00:24:44,416
Are you sure? Do you wanna, like…

498
00:24:44,500 --> 00:24:46,250
No, no, no. Sorry. What were you saying?

499
00:24:46,333 --> 00:24:47,750
Um…

500
00:24:47,833 --> 00:24:51,583
Erin. She invited me
to this protest the other day,

501
00:24:51,666 --> 00:24:55,875
and instead, I just sat in the auditorium
and did nothing for three hours.

502
00:24:55,958 --> 00:24:57,875
You mean when we blocked the opening?

503
00:24:58,375 --> 00:25:01,416
-I'm literally gonna be in the shadows.
-You look so cool.

504
00:25:01,500 --> 00:25:04,791
-I mean, I'm excited for you.
-I'm excited for both of us.

505
00:25:05,708 --> 00:25:07,750
I have one line, Sophie.

506
00:25:07,833 --> 00:25:12,125
And your solo in "Club Knocked Up."
Come on, it's sounding so good. Belt it.

507
00:25:14,250 --> 00:25:15,791
<i>♪ Knock knock ♪</i>

508
00:25:17,750 --> 00:25:18,958
Nailed it.

509
00:25:19,041 --> 00:25:20,958
-[Caleb] I'll get there first.
-[Ethan] I will.

510
00:25:21,041 --> 00:25:23,958
[Ted] Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!
Please, no running. Stop, don't move.

511
00:25:24,041 --> 00:25:26,458
Bring these to your friend Jeremy
and his dad.

512
00:25:26,541 --> 00:25:27,708
-Some of that.
-[Elizabeth] Hey.

513
00:25:27,791 --> 00:25:29,958
You really have to figure out
those driving lessons.

514
00:25:30,041 --> 00:25:32,125
Otherwise, you're gonna go off to college,

515
00:25:32,208 --> 00:25:35,041
and then you're gonna move
to New York and become a star,

516
00:25:35,125 --> 00:25:38,125
and then you'll be one of those
New Yorkers who never learned to drive.

517
00:25:38,208 --> 00:25:39,875
-I'll hire a hot chauffeur.
-[laughs]

518
00:25:39,958 --> 00:25:41,666
-[Ethan] No, Jeremy, stop!
-[woman] Just…

519
00:25:41,750 --> 00:25:43,166
-[Ethan] Jeremy, stop!
-What was that?

520
00:25:43,250 --> 00:25:45,500
-[Caleb] Gimme the pickle.
-[Ethan] I want that bagel!

521
00:25:45,583 --> 00:25:49,333
Okay, but what about when you fall in love
with your hot chauffeur

522
00:25:49,416 --> 00:25:53,041
and get married and have kids
and then you have to drive them to school?

523
00:25:53,666 --> 00:25:54,916
Why can't he drive them?

524
00:25:55,000 --> 00:25:58,291
Because you will be better at it
because I taught you how to drive.

525
00:25:58,375 --> 00:25:59,333
Mmm.

526
00:25:59,416 --> 00:26:01,166
Women's rights.

527
00:26:01,250 --> 00:26:02,750
Fine, teach me to drive.

528
00:26:02,833 --> 00:26:05,250
Okay. Tomorrow, after school?

529
00:26:05,333 --> 00:26:06,333
[Sophie] Uh, let me see.

530
00:26:07,375 --> 00:26:10,416
-Ugh. Shoot. Rehearsal.
-[Ted] You wanna wear the shoes?

531
00:26:10,500 --> 00:26:12,833
-You can't act like that. Come on.
-[Caleb] I'm telling Mom.

532
00:26:13,458 --> 00:26:15,250
[Elizabeth] Ugh, what happened?

533
00:26:15,333 --> 00:26:18,250
Ethan called Jeremy Silcox a dipshit.

534
00:26:18,791 --> 00:26:20,041
[Elizabeth laughs]

535
00:26:21,875 --> 00:26:23,625
-Wanna just go now?
-[Sophie] Yeah.

536
00:26:24,500 --> 00:26:26,583
-Some of the songs are really hard.
-Mmm.

537
00:26:26,666 --> 00:26:30,125
I've been listening to the recordings,
and she just… she sounds so good.

538
00:26:30,208 --> 00:26:32,166
-And I just--
-Yeah, 'cause it's a recording.

539
00:26:32,250 --> 00:26:34,000
You know, she had so many chances,

540
00:26:34,083 --> 00:26:37,541
and she had so much time to figure it out.

541
00:26:37,625 --> 00:26:39,500
You have time too, sweetie.

542
00:26:40,166 --> 00:26:41,416
[Sophie sighs]

543
00:26:42,500 --> 00:26:43,416
What?

544
00:26:43,500 --> 00:26:44,750
-[retches]
-Mom!

545
00:26:46,041 --> 00:26:47,333
-[Sophie] Oh…
-[Elizabeth gasps]

546
00:26:47,416 --> 00:26:49,583
Oh, don't look, honey. Please don't look.

547
00:26:49,666 --> 00:26:51,666
[coughing and gasping]

548
00:26:53,333 --> 00:26:54,875
Oh! [gasps]

549
00:26:54,958 --> 00:26:56,958
[breathing heavily]

550
00:26:57,875 --> 00:26:59,875
[gentle, poignant music playing]

551
00:27:07,875 --> 00:27:11,208
-[poignant music builds]
-[no in-scene audio]

552
00:27:18,041 --> 00:27:20,041
[music continues]

553
00:27:36,708 --> 00:27:38,708
[gentle music continues]

554
00:27:45,875 --> 00:27:47,291
[Elizabeth] <i>I know he said it's worse</i>

555
00:27:47,375 --> 00:27:50,333
<i>and spreading faster</i>
<i>than he thought it would, but…</i>

556
00:27:51,041 --> 00:27:53,041
Can't be happening that fast, right?

557
00:27:53,125 --> 00:27:54,666
Lizzie, I don't know.

558
00:27:54,750 --> 00:27:58,208
Maybe the end of July or August?

559
00:27:58,291 --> 00:28:00,833
He said he couldn't say.
I really… I don't think he knows.

560
00:28:00,916 --> 00:28:03,375
I know he said, you know,
travel isn't a good idea,

561
00:28:03,458 --> 00:28:05,916
but we can't not go to the beach house.

562
00:28:06,000 --> 00:28:08,166
-Yeah.
-I already told Sophie.

563
00:28:08,791 --> 00:28:11,875
Oh, God. And the show.
The show is so important to her.

564
00:28:12,458 --> 00:28:13,583
[sighs]

565
00:28:16,666 --> 00:28:18,291
Let's not tell them.

566
00:28:19,125 --> 00:28:20,625
Just not yet.

567
00:28:21,125 --> 00:28:22,541
Well, what about Soph?

568
00:28:22,625 --> 00:28:25,166
-She'll quit the show.
-She's gonna want to know.

569
00:28:25,250 --> 00:28:28,541
She has something that makes her happy,
and I can't let her lose that too.

570
00:28:28,625 --> 00:28:30,333
They're gonna see what's happening.

571
00:28:33,625 --> 00:28:38,000
Okay, we can tell them…
tell them that I'm struggling, but not…

572
00:28:41,125 --> 00:28:42,833
And then, after the show,

573
00:28:43,708 --> 00:28:45,208
we go to the Crane House.

574
00:28:45,291 --> 00:28:46,916
-We'll all be together.
-Okay.

575
00:28:47,500 --> 00:28:49,833
-And we can just tell them there.
-Great.

576
00:28:50,791 --> 00:28:54,416
I think, in the meantime,
we can ask my parents to come help.

577
00:28:54,500 --> 00:28:57,750
-Yeah. Whatever you want.
-Well, it's definitely not what I want.

578
00:28:57,833 --> 00:29:01,083
-Uh… I know.
-But I just… think we're gonna need them.

579
00:29:01,708 --> 00:29:02,875
But oh, my mom.

580
00:29:02,958 --> 00:29:04,208
[sighs]

581
00:29:04,291 --> 00:29:07,291
I'll take care of it.
Okay? I don't want you to worry.

582
00:29:07,375 --> 00:29:10,250
I mean, I kind of need
something to worry about that's not…

583
00:29:10,916 --> 00:29:12,458
that's not it.

584
00:29:15,750 --> 00:29:19,708
Is… "it" your mom?

585
00:29:20,500 --> 00:29:21,375
Or…

586
00:29:21,458 --> 00:29:23,708
It's my mom? Uh, it's the…

587
00:29:23,791 --> 00:29:26,708
-You… you said "it."
-It's the cancer.

588
00:29:28,166 --> 00:29:30,083
-I got… I got con…
-[laughs]

589
00:29:30,750 --> 00:29:32,208
I got confused.

590
00:29:33,083 --> 00:29:35,083
[phone ringing]

591
00:29:36,708 --> 00:29:39,666
-Hello?
-[Ted] <i>Maybe I'm hopped up on coffee and…</i>

592
00:29:39,750 --> 00:29:41,708
[Elizabeth laughs]

593
00:29:41,791 --> 00:29:42,625
Dad?

594
00:29:43,125 --> 00:29:47,416
[Elizabeth] <i>You thought I would say "it"?</i>
<i>You thought I would call her "it"?</i>

595
00:29:47,500 --> 00:29:49,875
-[laughing]
-[Ted] <i>I won't tell anybody.</i>

596
00:29:50,416 --> 00:29:51,666
<i>Especially it.</i>

597
00:29:51,750 --> 00:29:53,750
[Elizabeth and Ted laughing]

598
00:29:54,541 --> 00:29:56,041
-[laughs]
-[Elizabeth] <i>Yeah.</i>

599
00:29:57,000 --> 00:29:58,458
<i>Oh my God.</i>

600
00:29:59,083 --> 00:30:01,500
-[laughing] <i>Oh my God!</i>
-[Ted] <i>That's so cute.</i>

601
00:30:03,041 --> 00:30:04,291
[Elizabeth sighs]

602
00:30:05,166 --> 00:30:08,291
-I'm sure I got the wrong cheese.
-I think the cheese is fine.

603
00:30:08,375 --> 00:30:09,958
[Ethan] Mom, Mom, they're here!

604
00:30:13,916 --> 00:30:16,458
-Doorbell doesn't work.
-It's this one, Grandpa Dale.

605
00:30:16,541 --> 00:30:17,375
-[bell rings]
-Oh!

606
00:30:17,458 --> 00:30:19,333
Joke never gets old, huh, Dale?

607
00:30:19,416 --> 00:30:20,666
-Boys, quit it. Enough.
-Okay.

608
00:30:20,750 --> 00:30:23,125
-When did you get so big?
-[Ted] Hug your grandmother, please.

609
00:30:23,208 --> 00:30:24,541
Come over here, you!

610
00:30:24,625 --> 00:30:26,458
Oh! Oh my goodness.

611
00:30:26,541 --> 00:30:28,333
[Ted] All right, boys, inside. Let's go.

612
00:30:29,833 --> 00:30:30,833
Oh!

613
00:30:31,541 --> 00:30:34,791
-Excuse me, who is this woman?
-[laughs]

614
00:30:34,875 --> 00:30:37,583
-Sophie, you're so gorgeous.
-Thank you.

615
00:30:37,666 --> 00:30:40,791
-Oh, God. Where's your mother?
-She's right there.

616
00:30:41,375 --> 00:30:44,125
-[grandmother] Oh, my baby.
-Hi, Mom.

617
00:30:46,500 --> 00:30:49,333
[Caleb] Why are Grandpa Dale and Lala
staying in my room?

618
00:30:49,416 --> 00:30:51,333
[Ted] Because you only
sleep in Ethan's room.

619
00:30:51,416 --> 00:30:53,625
Yeah, but why do I have
to sleep on the trundle?

620
00:30:53,708 --> 00:30:56,166
You literally refuse
to sleep anyplace else.

621
00:30:56,250 --> 00:30:57,791
How long are they staying?

622
00:30:58,500 --> 00:31:00,458
-[grandmother] Uh…
-Um, we don't know.

623
00:31:00,541 --> 00:31:03,958
Yeah, and your mom said I might be able
to give you driving lessons?

624
00:31:04,041 --> 00:31:06,375
Yeah, that'd be fun. Totally.

625
00:31:08,333 --> 00:31:11,125
-Well, you guys must be starving.
-Come on, boys, let's go upstairs.

626
00:31:11,208 --> 00:31:13,750
-Bring the bags.
-[Ethan] I wanna carry Grandpa's suitcase.

627
00:31:13,833 --> 00:31:15,416
-[Caleb] No, I do! I do!
-[grandmother] Oh.

628
00:31:15,500 --> 00:31:16,958
[Ted] Forget where the stairs are?

629
00:31:17,041 --> 00:31:20,041
Oh. Oh. Well, uh…

630
00:31:20,833 --> 00:31:24,000
I'm off creamy cheeses.
It's not good for my gut.

631
00:31:24,083 --> 00:31:25,041
Oh.

632
00:31:27,458 --> 00:31:28,333
[Dale] But, um…

633
00:31:28,916 --> 00:31:29,833
I'll have a grape.

634
00:31:29,916 --> 00:31:31,833
-Just a grape?
-[Dale] Yeah. Whoa.

635
00:31:33,791 --> 00:31:34,708
Thank you.

636
00:31:36,333 --> 00:31:37,500
Just one grape?

637
00:31:37,583 --> 00:31:40,125
So after you come back
in the door, Sophie,

638
00:31:40,208 --> 00:31:42,750
um, you grab him,
and that's where the kiss happens.

639
00:31:43,541 --> 00:31:44,791
[whispers] Where's Carolyn?

640
00:31:46,000 --> 00:31:48,250
Do you feel okay about that, Sophie?

641
00:31:48,916 --> 00:31:51,000
Oh, uh… I don't know.

642
00:31:51,750 --> 00:31:55,208
[Ms. Parker] Well, we can do something
other than a kiss. Like a hug or…

643
00:31:55,708 --> 00:31:57,375
-Jack, what do you think?
-Oh, uh…

644
00:31:57,458 --> 00:32:00,125
-I did a kiss last year. I'm cool.
-Yeah. I'm cool too, then.

645
00:32:00,208 --> 00:32:02,541
Okay, great. So why don't we try one?

646
00:32:03,166 --> 00:32:04,125
Okay.

647
00:32:13,500 --> 00:32:14,875
[door slams loudly]

648
00:32:18,166 --> 00:32:20,125
Sophie, you have to kiss him.

649
00:32:20,625 --> 00:32:21,708
Yes.

650
00:32:41,375 --> 00:32:42,291
[Ms. Parker] Good.

651
00:32:43,416 --> 00:32:47,041
The thing is, right now, Jenna is thinking
she's made a huge mistake,

652
00:32:47,125 --> 00:32:48,708
so maybe, mmm…

653
00:32:49,416 --> 00:32:50,250
less smiley.

654
00:32:50,333 --> 00:32:51,166
Oh.

655
00:32:51,666 --> 00:32:55,000
Yeah. Um, sorry,
I was just trying an acting choice.

656
00:32:55,083 --> 00:32:56,666
Yeah? Great.

657
00:32:57,458 --> 00:32:59,333
-Do you wanna try it again?
-Yes.

658
00:33:01,958 --> 00:33:03,958
["She Used to Be Mine" playing
through earbuds]

659
00:33:04,041 --> 00:33:07,500
[grandmother] …Dale and I to come here
and say, "Let's straighten this out."

660
00:33:07,583 --> 00:33:09,208
No, listen to me.

661
00:33:09,291 --> 00:33:12,166
Our neighbor can get her into Dana-Farber.

662
00:33:12,250 --> 00:33:14,666
Their cancer team
is top three in the country.

663
00:33:14,750 --> 00:33:17,541
-[Ted] That's what all the hospitals say.
-[grandmother] They really are.

664
00:33:17,625 --> 00:33:19,666
[Ted] Listen. We're doing
everything that we can.

665
00:33:19,750 --> 00:33:21,625
We trust Dr. Steckman and his team.

666
00:33:21,708 --> 00:33:24,083
-Who is Dr. Steckman? What hospital is--
-[Ted] You know him!

667
00:33:24,166 --> 00:33:27,000
-[grandmother] I've never met the man.
-[Ted] The same doctor from last time!

668
00:33:27,083 --> 00:33:29,541
-[buzz of conversation]
-[girl] Right. So, um…

669
00:33:30,666 --> 00:33:33,083
I can't believe I missed you guys kissing.

670
00:33:33,166 --> 00:33:35,708
I'm telling you,
the chemistry was undeniable.

671
00:33:35,791 --> 00:33:37,916
Okay, remember when we made out
with those guys at camp,

672
00:33:38,000 --> 00:33:41,541
and we were like, "Ew, it's so slimy,"
and we didn't get what the big deal was?

673
00:33:41,625 --> 00:33:44,916
I get what the big deal is now. Like,
We were just kissing the wrong people.

674
00:33:45,000 --> 00:33:47,208
Hey, Carolyn, you forgot this.

675
00:33:47,291 --> 00:33:48,625
[Carolyn] Oh, thanks.

676
00:33:48,708 --> 00:33:50,791
My legs are killing me from yesterday.

677
00:33:50,875 --> 00:33:52,416
-You?
-Yesterday?

678
00:33:53,041 --> 00:33:56,875
Yeah, we did this hike after school.
I thought it was gonna be like two miles,

679
00:33:56,958 --> 00:33:59,791
and then it ended up
being four and a half miles.

680
00:33:59,875 --> 00:34:00,750
Cool.

681
00:34:01,750 --> 00:34:02,625
Yeah.

682
00:34:04,041 --> 00:34:06,333
You should totally come with us next time.

683
00:34:06,416 --> 00:34:07,916
Thank you, that's sweet.

684
00:34:09,833 --> 00:34:11,500
You told me
you had a doctor's appointment.

685
00:34:11,583 --> 00:34:14,000
I had to get a ride home
with Trista and her mom.

686
00:34:15,000 --> 00:34:16,333
Wait, are you quitting the show?

687
00:34:18,708 --> 00:34:20,333
I already did.

688
00:34:20,916 --> 00:34:22,333
And you didn't tell me?

689
00:34:23,250 --> 00:34:25,458
-I don't know. I didn't know how.
-I am so sorry.

690
00:34:25,541 --> 00:34:27,708
-I didn't know. Yeah.
-It's okay. Can you just give us…

691
00:34:29,875 --> 00:34:31,833
You have a lot going on, so I--

692
00:34:31,916 --> 00:34:34,916
Yeah, you're right, I do have
a lot going on right now. I need to focus.

693
00:34:35,000 --> 00:34:37,208
-Soph, I wanted to--
-Don't worry about driving me anymore.

694
00:34:37,291 --> 00:34:40,708
My grandpa's just sitting around all day
with nothing to do. He loves to drive.

695
00:34:40,791 --> 00:34:41,708
Sophie!

696
00:34:43,666 --> 00:34:46,250
I need more practice.
Can we do extra rehearsals?

697
00:34:46,333 --> 00:34:47,333
Mmm…

698
00:34:47,416 --> 00:34:50,708
I'd rather devote my spare time
to lesson plans about Mesopotamia

699
00:34:50,791 --> 00:34:53,750
and the spice trade routes
along the Tigris and Euphrates rivers.

700
00:34:53,833 --> 00:34:54,791
Okay.

701
00:34:56,208 --> 00:34:58,458
I'm kidding! That's so boring!

702
00:34:59,166 --> 00:35:00,750
Yes, of course.

703
00:35:00,833 --> 00:35:03,166
Oh, um, I shouldn't have said it's boring.

704
00:35:03,250 --> 00:35:06,083
-Please don't tell Principal Howard.
-Yeah, of course not.

705
00:35:10,625 --> 00:35:13,125
<i>♪ It's a bad idea, me and you ♪</i>

706
00:35:13,208 --> 00:35:14,666
I know, I totally agree.

707
