00:58:53,916 --> 00:58:54,916
You okay?

1164
00:58:55,000 --> 00:58:56,166
Yeah.

1165
00:58:56,250 --> 00:59:00,500
I just… I really wanted to do a good job
for someone, but they can't come.

1166
00:59:00,583 --> 00:59:04,166
A lot of other people will be here,
so you could do a good job for them.

1167
00:59:04,958 --> 00:59:07,375
-Yeah.
-[Ms. Parker] Or maybe just for you.

1168
00:59:08,333 --> 00:59:11,916
You know, I cast you because
I saw something in your callback.

1169
00:59:12,000 --> 00:59:15,375
And you've worked hard,
and it shows, but what I saw,

1170
00:59:16,208 --> 00:59:18,166
ooh, we can't work for that.

1171
00:59:18,250 --> 00:59:19,916
You either got it or you don't.

1172
00:59:20,708 --> 00:59:22,291
You got it, Birenbaum.

1173
00:59:23,541 --> 00:59:25,458
You just gotta remember where you put it.

1174
00:59:28,708 --> 00:59:30,041
Are you done?

1175
00:59:30,625 --> 00:59:32,791
What was it you said you wanted again?

1176
00:59:32,875 --> 00:59:34,666
[loud chatter]

1177
00:59:34,750 --> 00:59:35,833
[Ms. Parker] You'll lock up?

1178
00:59:35,916 --> 00:59:39,458
-[Owen] I'm on it.
-All right. Please get some rest, okay?

1179
00:59:39,541 --> 00:59:42,750
I want you to have lots of energy
for your dress rehearsal tomorrow.

1180
00:59:42,833 --> 00:59:45,416
-[Mr. Stewart] Good night.
-May the theater gods bless your sleep.

1181
00:59:45,500 --> 00:59:47,666
-[TJ] Yes, thank you, Ms. Parker.
-[Mallory] Good night.

1182
00:59:47,750 --> 00:59:48,583
[TJ] Appreciate you.

1183
00:59:48,666 --> 00:59:50,125
[Owen] Yeah, I'll lock up.

1184
00:59:50,208 --> 00:59:52,166
After tech night after hours!

1185
00:59:52,250 --> 00:59:53,250
[cheering]

1186
00:59:53,333 --> 00:59:56,041
["Tornado Warnings"
by Sabrina Carpenter playing]

1187
00:59:56,125 --> 00:59:58,583
[TJ] All right, all right, all right,
we all know the drill.

1188
00:59:58,666 --> 01:00:02,041
Phones in here, because tonight is sacred.

1189
01:00:02,125 --> 01:00:04,000
-So let's do it!
-[cheering]

1190
01:00:04,083 --> 01:00:05,541
<i>♪ Our relationship arc ♪</i>

1191
01:00:05,625 --> 01:00:07,708
<i>♪ Ignoring tornado warnings ♪</i>

1192
01:00:07,791 --> 01:00:11,208
<i>-♪ Don't understand how quickly we get ♪</i>
-[TJ] Thanks, Sophie.

1193
01:00:11,291 --> 01:00:15,125
<i>♪ Right back in our rhythm</i>
<i>Without missin' a step ♪</i>

1194
01:00:15,208 --> 01:00:19,333
<i>♪ And logically the last thing</i>
<i>I should have on my mind ♪</i>

1195
01:00:19,416 --> 01:00:21,583
<i>-♪ But I want you there sometimes ♪</i>
-[Sophie] No!

1196
01:00:21,666 --> 01:00:22,875
-We dug it.
-We--

1197
01:00:22,958 --> 01:00:24,875
<i>♪ I guess maybe that's why </i>♪

1198
01:00:24,958 --> 01:00:29,958
♪ <i>I'm lyin' to my therapist </i>♪

1199
01:00:31,083 --> 01:00:33,500
<i>♪ I keep sayin' things like ♪</i>

1200
01:00:33,583 --> 01:00:38,458
<i>♪ "I never saw him and we never kissed" ♪</i>

1201
01:00:38,541 --> 01:00:40,625
-In the name of Shakespeare…
<i>-♪ Sondheim ♪</i>

1202
01:00:40,708 --> 01:00:43,250
-[TJ] And Lin-Manuel…
-[Owen] We all sign the wall.

1203
01:00:43,333 --> 01:00:48,500
Thus, all who come after us
shall know the glory that was…

1204
01:00:48,583 --> 01:00:50,958
[all yell] <i>Waitress</i>!

1205
01:00:51,041 --> 01:00:52,166
[cheering and whistling]

1206
01:00:52,250 --> 01:00:54,416
<i>♪ To my therapist… ♪</i>

1207
01:00:54,500 --> 01:00:57,291
Okay, come get your Sharpies!
I'm signing first.

1208
01:00:57,375 --> 01:00:59,500
<i>-♪ I deserve an hour in a week ♪</i>
-[TJ] Yeah!

1209
01:01:00,083 --> 01:01:01,500
<i>-♪ To focus on my thoughts ♪</i>
-[TJ] Yes!

1210
01:01:01,583 --> 01:01:05,208
<i>♪ Not so obsessed with yours</i>
<i>I can't hear myself speak ♪</i>

1211
01:01:05,958 --> 01:01:08,291
<i>♪ I deserve my own consideration ♪</i>

1212
01:01:08,375 --> 01:01:10,375
<i>♪ Sometimes, I wish I kept ♪</i>

1213
01:01:10,458 --> 01:01:12,500
<i>♪ Some of my feelings in the basement ♪</i>

1214
01:01:12,583 --> 01:01:14,583
<i>♪ So I'd still have some left ♪</i>

1215
01:01:14,666 --> 01:01:17,541
<i>♪ Don't understand how quickly we get ♪</i>

1216
01:01:18,125 --> 01:01:21,750
<i>♪ Right back in our rhythm</i>
<i>Without missin' a step ♪</i>

1217
01:01:21,833 --> 01:01:25,750
<i>♪ And logically the last thing</i>
<i>I should have on my mind ♪</i>

1218
01:01:25,833 --> 01:01:28,583
<i>♪ But I want you there sometimes ♪</i>

1219
01:01:31,458 --> 01:01:32,291
[TJ] <i>So.</i>

1220
01:01:33,708 --> 01:01:35,750
Who do we think's gonna hook up tonight?

1221
01:01:36,500 --> 01:01:39,875
[girl] Lots of possibilities.
Anything could happen.

1222
01:01:39,958 --> 01:01:42,333
Mike and Becca are already gone.

1223
01:01:42,416 --> 01:01:43,500
-Stop!
-Mike and…

1224
01:01:43,583 --> 01:01:44,458
-Really?
-[girl] I know!

1225
01:01:44,541 --> 01:01:47,375
-They just left the auditorium.
-[Jack] I'm gonna head to the bathroom.

1226
01:01:48,291 --> 01:01:49,208
Have fun.

1227
01:01:49,291 --> 01:01:51,000
Gonna have the time of my life.

1228
01:01:51,083 --> 01:01:52,833
Top ten bathroom experience?

1229
01:01:53,916 --> 01:01:55,041
Top five.

1230
01:01:55,125 --> 01:01:56,500
Think big, Birenbaum.

1231
01:01:56,583 --> 01:01:58,583
[soft, relaxed music playing]

1232
01:01:59,083 --> 01:02:01,541
-Just don't throw up on him. [laughs]
-Stop.

1233
01:02:03,708 --> 01:02:05,375
Go. Go, go.

1234
01:02:36,333 --> 01:02:37,791
[sighs]

1235
01:02:53,125 --> 01:02:54,125
[music fades]

1236
01:02:59,666 --> 01:03:02,666
"Hey, I had to go to the bathroom too.
Similar bladders!"

1237
01:03:02,750 --> 01:03:04,375
Ew, don't say the last part.

1238
01:03:12,041 --> 01:03:13,375
I have a boyfriend.

1239
01:03:13,458 --> 01:03:16,125
Right, from Stage Door Manor.

1240
01:03:16,208 --> 01:03:18,333
[Mallory] Don't say it like that.

1241
01:03:18,416 --> 01:03:21,708
It's very prestigious.
My boyfriend's a great actor.

1242
01:03:23,875 --> 01:03:26,375
Stage Door Manor? Absolutely!

1243
01:03:30,666 --> 01:03:31,708
So?

1244
01:03:32,666 --> 01:03:33,791
[Sophie] Mm-mm.

1245
01:03:33,875 --> 01:03:34,708
Oh.

1246
01:03:35,708 --> 01:03:36,708
Uh…

1247
01:03:38,041 --> 01:03:39,875
Oh, I don't know if you wanna go back in.

1248
01:03:39,958 --> 01:03:42,041
Uh, it turned into a make-out den.

1249
01:03:42,125 --> 01:03:44,916
Trista's eating Fishman's face.

1250
01:03:46,750 --> 01:03:49,166
-Yeah, sounds messy.
-Mmm.

1251
01:03:50,583 --> 01:03:52,000
At least you get a stage kiss.

1252
01:03:52,083 --> 01:03:53,875
I give my life to this program every year.

1253
01:03:53,958 --> 01:03:56,000
I've never even gotten
to fake kiss anyone.

1254
01:03:59,708 --> 01:04:00,916
[Sophie sighs]

1255
01:04:04,500 --> 01:04:06,708
-No.
-No. [chuckles]

1256
01:04:18,250 --> 01:04:19,375
[Sophie] Thank you.

1257
01:04:25,250 --> 01:04:26,125
[Jack] Birenbaum.

1258
01:04:26,625 --> 01:04:27,458
Need a ride?

1259
01:04:35,208 --> 01:04:36,583
-Thank you.
-[chuckles]

1260
01:04:36,666 --> 01:04:39,500
Are you nervous for tomorrow?
'Cause I'm so nervous.

1261
01:04:39,583 --> 01:04:40,958
I didn't know you get nervous.

1262
01:04:41,041 --> 01:04:42,875
I still feel like
I'm not fully off book yet.

1263
01:04:42,958 --> 01:04:45,750
You're gonna be great, Jack.
You're always great.

1264
01:04:50,583 --> 01:04:52,083
Are we practicing again?

1265
01:04:53,208 --> 01:04:55,416
You were just kissing Mallory.

1266
01:04:55,916 --> 01:04:57,458
I… I thought you liked me.

1267
01:04:57,541 --> 01:05:00,083
I'm starting to think you only
do the plays to kiss all the girls,

1268
01:05:00,166 --> 01:05:02,041
which is honestly kind of sad.

1269
01:05:05,041 --> 01:05:06,708
I'm done kissing the wrong guys.

1270
01:05:10,833 --> 01:05:13,041
Let's not let this affect the show, okay?

1271
01:05:16,458 --> 01:05:17,750
[starts engine]

1272
01:05:20,250 --> 01:05:22,250
[phone plays sound of rooster crowing]

1273
01:05:30,666 --> 01:05:32,875
When do you think
they'll announce next year's show?

1274
01:05:32,958 --> 01:05:34,333
-Probably tonight.
-[Mallory trills]

1275
01:05:34,416 --> 01:05:35,875
-[laughing] Tonight?
-[Mallory trills]

1276
01:05:35,958 --> 01:05:37,625
-[trills] Ahem.
-[Sophie singing]

1277
01:05:37,708 --> 01:05:39,791
-[sliding] Ma! Ma!
-[Sophie humming]

1278
01:05:39,875 --> 01:05:41,500
Ma! Ahem.

1279
01:05:42,083 --> 01:05:44,083
[Mallory trills]

1280
01:05:45,291 --> 01:05:47,083
{\an8}-[piano playing]
-[boy] Left… No…

1281
01:05:47,166 --> 01:05:48,791
{\an8}[Ms. Parker] Hi, Mrs. Birenbaum.

1282
01:05:48,875 --> 01:05:51,166
{\an8}<i>-Hi.</i>
-[girl] What's the time?

1283
01:05:51,250 --> 01:05:53,666
{\an8}<i>Hey, thank you so much</i>
<i>for letting me watch.</i>

1284
01:05:53,750 --> 01:05:55,416
I am so glad you reached out.

1285
01:05:55,500 --> 01:05:57,625
<i>And she's not gonna know, right?</i>

1286
01:05:57,708 --> 01:05:59,208
<i>No. No.</i>

1287
01:06:00,041 --> 01:06:03,916
Thank you for… everything
that you've been doing with Sophie.

1288
01:06:04,000 --> 01:06:08,125
It's been so amazing
to see her working so hard.

1289
01:06:08,208 --> 01:06:10,875
TJ, you are so late. Get backstage.

1290
01:06:10,958 --> 01:06:13,291
Sorry, my Yoo-hoo exploded in my backpack.

1291
01:06:13,375 --> 01:06:15,833
-I don't care. Go!
-[TJ] Okay, I'm going! Okay.

1292
01:06:15,916 --> 01:06:17,416
[Fishman] Bro, double-check the levels.

1293
01:06:17,500 --> 01:06:19,000
[boy 1] Okay, checking…

1294
01:06:19,083 --> 01:06:20,083
-Uh…
-[boy 1] Sounds good.

1295
01:06:20,166 --> 01:06:22,375
<i>-She is amazing.</i>
-Yeah.

1296
01:06:22,958 --> 01:06:25,000
<i>I had no idea things were so…</i>

1297
01:06:29,583 --> 01:06:32,291
[cast] One, two, three!
One, two, three! One, two, three!

1298
01:06:32,375 --> 01:06:34,083
One, two! One, two! One, two! One, two!

1299
01:06:34,166 --> 01:06:35,291
One! One! One! One!

1300
01:06:35,375 --> 01:06:37,333
[whooping and cheering]

1301
01:06:37,416 --> 01:06:38,708
-[Mr. Stewart] Okay.
-All right.

1302
01:06:38,791 --> 01:06:41,375
Give it your all, okay?
I know it's just a dress rehearsal,

1303
01:06:41,458 --> 01:06:45,166
but you never know if a Broadway
casting director might be watching.

1304
01:06:45,250 --> 01:06:47,250
[all] Ooh!

1305
01:06:47,916 --> 01:06:50,166
[boy] Hey, Broadway! Hey, Broadway!

1306
01:06:50,250 --> 01:06:51,125
[cast chattering]

1307
01:06:51,208 --> 01:06:53,500
[Mallory] Where is everybody?
Get to your sides, everybody!

1308
01:06:55,666 --> 01:06:56,625
Hey, what time…

1309
01:06:56,708 --> 01:06:58,416
Get to your sides. All right?

1310
01:07:01,916 --> 01:07:03,250
[girl 1] <i>♪ Sugar ♪</i>

1311
01:07:04,291 --> 01:07:05,416
<i>♪ Sugar ♪</i>

1312
01:07:06,583 --> 01:07:10,500
<i>♪ Sugar, butter, sugar, butter ♪</i>

1313
01:07:11,000 --> 01:07:13,083
<i>-♪ Sugar, butter ♪</i>
-[girl 2] <i>♪ Flour ♪</i>

1314
01:07:13,166 --> 01:07:15,583
<i>-♪ Sugar, butter ♪</i>
<i>-♪ Flour ♪</i>

1315
01:07:15,666 --> 01:07:17,583
<i>-♪ Sugar, butter ♪</i>
<i>-♪ Flour ♪</i>

1316
01:07:17,666 --> 01:07:20,083
<i>-♪ Sugar, butter ♪</i>
<i>-♪ Flour ♪</i>

1317
01:07:20,166 --> 01:07:23,291
<i>♪ My hands pluck the things</i>
<i>I know that I'll need ♪</i>

1318
01:07:23,375 --> 01:07:25,458
<i>-♪ Flour ♪</i>
<i>-♪ I take the sugar and butter ♪</i>

1319
01:07:25,541 --> 01:07:27,833
<i>-♪ From the pantry ♪</i>
<i>-♪ Sugar, butter ♪</i>

1320
01:07:27,916 --> 01:07:32,583
<i>♪ I add the flour to begin</i>
<i>What I'm hoping to start ♪</i>

1321
01:07:32,666 --> 01:07:37,500
<i>♪ And then it's down with the recipe</i>
<i>And bake from the heart ♪</i>

1322
01:07:37,583 --> 01:07:41,333
<i>-♪ Sugar ♪</i>
<i>-♪ Ooh, ooh, sugar, butter ♪</i>

1323
01:07:42,083 --> 01:07:46,000
<i>-♪ And butter ♪</i>
<i>-♪ Sugar, butter ♪</i>

1324
01:07:46,583 --> 01:07:50,500
<i>-♪ And flour ♪</i>
<i>-♪ Sugar, butter ♪</i>

1325
01:07:51,000 --> 01:07:52,291
-[boy] Oh!
-[Mallory squeals]

1326
01:07:52,375 --> 01:07:53,291
[gasps]

1327
01:07:53,375 --> 01:07:54,916
[Ms. Parker] <i>Everybody okay?</i>

1328
01:07:55,000 --> 01:07:56,416
Hey, sorry!

1329
01:07:56,916 --> 01:07:59,500
-You good, Sophie?
-[Sophie] Yeah. We're good. Thank you.

1330
01:07:59,583 --> 01:08:02,166
Okay, so let's just take a minute
and take care of that, please.

1331
01:08:02,250 --> 01:08:04,291
[Owen] One more time. Clean it up.

1332
01:08:04,375 --> 01:08:07,625
-This run-through sucks.
-Bad run-through means great show.

1333
01:08:07,708 --> 01:08:11,666
-Did you see the computer and camera?
-Is Ms. Parker, like, live streaming it?

1334
01:08:11,750 --> 01:08:14,083
I heard someone's watching
from their couch.

1335
01:08:14,166 --> 01:08:15,666
-Weird.
-Who do you think it is?

1336
01:08:16,583 --> 01:08:20,291
Isn't it obvious?
A Broadway casting director.

1337
01:08:20,375 --> 01:08:21,916
-[laughter]
-Could you imagine?

1338
01:08:23,333 --> 01:08:27,541
"What Baking Can Do" was, um…
really emotionally resonant today.

1339
01:08:28,125 --> 01:08:31,416
-[knock at door]
-Back in two minutes, people. Back in two.

1340
01:08:31,500 --> 01:08:32,750
Thank you, two.

1341
01:08:34,041 --> 01:08:35,708
You're doing a good job.

1342
01:08:36,375 --> 01:08:37,666
-[knocking]
-[Jack] Sophie.

1343
01:08:37,750 --> 01:08:38,625
Yeah.

1344
01:08:43,958 --> 01:08:46,875
You ready for act two? We're good, right?

1345
01:08:46,958 --> 01:08:48,750
I just wanted to say,

1346
01:08:49,375 --> 01:08:50,375
uh, I'm so sorry.

1347
01:08:51,291 --> 01:08:52,875
I heard your mom's really sick.

1348
01:08:53,375 --> 01:08:56,625
TJ said that he saw
your mom talking to Ms. Parker.

1349
01:08:57,791 --> 01:08:59,750
My… my parents got divorced
a few years ago. Um…

1350
01:08:59,833 --> 01:09:03,291
I'm not saying it's the same.
Um, it's not, but…

1351
01:09:04,000 --> 01:09:07,208
Just… let me know
if I can be there for you, okay?

1352
01:09:12,000 --> 01:09:14,958
We wouldn't have sucked so bad
if we'd known she was watching.

1353
01:09:15,041 --> 01:09:17,166
[Trista] I'm really sorry, Sophie.

1354
01:09:21,291 --> 01:09:22,541
[Fishman] Lights up.

1355
01:09:23,666 --> 01:09:26,958
Sorry, it's a little messy,
but Sophie's doing so great.

1356
01:09:27,041 --> 01:09:29,708
-No, thank you, it's wonderful.
-[Fishman] <i>Ms. Parker?</i>

1357
01:09:31,000 --> 01:09:33,625
<i>Carl is locked</i>
<i>in the spotlight booth again.</i>

1358
01:09:33,708 --> 01:09:34,708
[Ms. Parker] <i>What? Ugh!</i>

1359
01:09:34,791 --> 01:09:38,541
-I told you to give him the keys.
-[Fishman] I didn't think it'd happen ag--

1360
01:09:39,333 --> 01:09:41,333
[piano playing "She Used To Be Mine"]

1361
01:09:46,166 --> 01:09:49,291
{\an8}-[Sophie] <i>♪ It's not simple to say ♪</i>
-Shoot.

1362
01:09:49,375 --> 01:09:52,208
{\an8}-Oh.
<i>-♪ That most days ♪</i>

1363
01:09:52,708 --> 01:09:54,208
-[Elizabeth] <i>Ted!</i>
-[Sophie] <i>♪ I… ♪</i>

1364
01:09:56,083 --> 01:09:57,166
[Elizabeth] <i>Ted!</i>

1365
01:09:59,708 --> 01:10:01,000
<i>Hey, Ted?</i>

1366
01:10:07,250 --> 01:10:08,916
-[sobbing]
-[Ted] Hey, hey, hey.

1367
01:10:09,000 --> 01:10:11,541
What's going on? What's… what's wrong?

1368
01:10:13,875 --> 01:10:14,750
What?

1369
01:10:15,625 --> 01:10:17,625
[sobbing]

1370
01:10:17,708 --> 01:10:19,541
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey, hey.

1371
01:10:20,041 --> 01:10:22,375
It's okay, Sophie.

1372
01:10:22,458 --> 01:10:23,750
-It's okay.
-I'm so sorry.

1373
01:10:23,833 --> 01:10:25,916
-No, I'm sorry. And you're doing great.
-No, I…

1374
01:10:26,000 --> 01:10:29,875
-Hey! You are doing great, okay?
-[sniffles]

1375
01:10:29,958 --> 01:10:31,625
Why don't you go home, huh?

1376
01:10:31,708 --> 01:10:34,166
-[whimpers]
-And come back fresh tomorrow for opening.

1377
01:10:34,250 --> 01:10:35,833
-Okay.
-Okay?

1378
01:10:39,666 --> 01:10:41,083
I wish you didn't do that.

1379
01:10:41,166 --> 01:10:43,666
-I just wanted to see you. I'm sorry.
-Mom, you should've asked me!

1380
01:10:43,750 --> 01:10:45,625
I… I didn't want to get your hopes up.

1381
01:10:45,708 --> 01:10:48,666
-In case I was feeling too sick.
-You can talk to me! I'm not a little kid!

1382
01:10:48,750 --> 01:10:51,083
I know. I know that.
You're growing up so fast.

1383
01:10:51,166 --> 01:10:56,208
-I feel like I'm… missing so much--
-Mom, you told me to do the show!

1384
01:10:56,291 --> 01:10:59,750
I did, yes, and of course
you should have done the show.

1385
01:10:59,833 --> 01:11:01,500
But I didn't know you were…

1386
01:11:01,583 --> 01:11:02,625
[sobs]

1387
01:11:03,791 --> 01:11:06,458
-You didn't tell me.
-I wanted to fight it.

1388
01:11:06,541 --> 01:11:10,250
I wanted to fight it,
and I tried so hard. I've been trying.

1389
01:11:10,333 --> 01:11:13,000
If you had told me, I wouldn't have
worked so much on the show.

1390
01:11:13,083 --> 01:11:17,666
You were so excited about it, honey.
I didn't want to ruin it for you.

1391
01:11:17,750 --> 01:11:19,375
You should have let <i>me </i>choose!

1392
01:11:19,458 --> 01:11:21,958
-You're right.
-I asked for extra rehearsals.

1393
01:11:22,041 --> 01:11:23,750
-Oh, honey.
-I'm not good enough.

1394
01:11:23,833 --> 01:11:26,000
-And I didn't wanna be around here.
-You're great.

1395
01:11:26,083 --> 01:11:28,916
-And me and Carolyn have been so weird.
-What happened with Carolyn?

1396
01:11:29,000 --> 01:11:31,708
-And now everything's awful.
-Honey.

1397
01:11:32,916 --> 01:11:35,958
Honey, I know things are hard. I know.

1398
01:11:36,041 --> 01:11:39,708
But… but, please…
You… you're so wonderful.

1399
01:11:39,791 --> 01:11:42,791
-Mom, do not lie about that too.
-I'm not lying!

1400
01:11:42,875 --> 01:11:45,500
-I'm not lying.
-Yes, you are! It's terrible! I'm terrible!

1401
01:11:45,583 --> 01:11:48,625
-No. No, no, no. Honey, no.
-[sobbing]

1402
01:11:48,708 --> 01:11:51,458
Listen to me.
Sophie, just look at me, okay?

1403
01:11:52,958 --> 01:11:55,791
I'm so sorry I didn't tell you.

1404
01:11:58,083 --> 01:11:59,750
I don't know how to do this.

1405
01:12:00,333 --> 01:12:02,041
-Mom, just…
-It's hard.

1406
01:12:02,125 --> 01:12:03,166
Just say it.

1407
01:12:03,250 --> 01:12:04,333
[sighs]

1408
01:12:06,125 --> 01:12:07,958
-Sophie.
-Say it.

1409
01:12:09,708 --> 01:12:10,708
[sighs]

1410
01:12:13,583 --> 01:12:15,416
I'm not gonna make it.

1411
01:12:17,125 --> 01:12:19,041
[sobbing] No, no, no.

1412
01:12:21,291 --> 01:12:22,541
No.

1413
01:12:23,125 --> 01:12:24,166
[Elizabeth] Hey.

1414
01:12:29,833 --> 01:12:30,875
[sniffles]

1415
01:12:30,958 --> 01:12:32,958
[sobbing]

1416
01:12:36,875 --> 01:12:39,333
-[sighs]
-[footsteps going upstairs]

1417
01:12:43,166 --> 01:12:44,333
[sighs]

1418
01:12:44,416 --> 01:12:46,291
[emotional, somber music playing]

1419
01:13:00,916 --> 01:13:02,375
[birdsong]

1420
01:13:22,583 --> 01:13:25,041
[whispers] Can you wake up, please? Buddy.

1421
01:13:25,958 --> 01:13:26,958
Wake up.

1422
01:13:27,541 --> 01:13:30,875
Hi, how'd you sleep? Good morning.

1423
01:13:53,166 --> 01:13:55,583
-[Sophie] Bye. Love you.
-[Caleb] Bye, Sophie. Bye, Dad.

1424
01:13:55,666 --> 01:13:58,375
You good? You've got everything? Goodbye.

1425
01:13:59,041 --> 01:14:01,041
[school bell rings][sighs heavily]

1426
01:14:12,458 --> 01:14:13,583
You okay?

1427
01:14:15,458 --> 01:14:16,541
No.

1428
01:14:17,708 --> 01:14:18,791
Are you?

1429
01:14:20,250 --> 01:14:22,250
[sighs heavily]

1430
01:14:25,291 --> 01:14:26,166
No.

1431
01:14:27,625 --> 01:14:30,416
Soph, everything that's happening
is so unfair.

1432
01:14:32,500 --> 01:14:35,875
It's unfair for you, for me,
for your brothers, for Mom.

1433
01:14:35,958 --> 01:14:38,250
-[sniffles]
-Yeah.

1434
01:14:38,333 --> 01:14:41,666
I know all she's trying to do
is make it hurt less, but I don't…

1435
01:14:45,333 --> 01:14:46,916
I don't think that's possible.

1436
01:14:49,083 --> 01:14:50,291
[sniffles]

1437
01:14:50,375 --> 01:14:54,500
And I so wish we could just fast-forward
to the part where you forgive us, but…

1438
01:14:55,250 --> 01:14:57,333
I know that's not possible either.

1439
01:14:58,541 --> 01:15:00,041
I hate you're going through this,

1440
01:15:00,125 --> 01:15:03,125
because every time I look at you,
all I see is how much I love you.

1441
01:15:07,833 --> 01:15:09,458
It's what Mom sees too.

1442
01:15:22,041 --> 01:15:23,458
[music fades]

1443
01:15:23,541 --> 01:15:25,583
[Carolyn] I'm with you for all of it.

1444
01:15:26,458 --> 01:15:28,708
No matter what, okay?

1445
01:15:32,333 --> 01:15:35,291
Also, I got you something.

1446
01:15:39,208 --> 01:15:40,500
[laughs]

1447
01:15:40,583 --> 01:15:45,083
I know I'm not in the play, but it doesn't
mean that all the traditions have to end.

1448
01:15:45,583 --> 01:15:47,250
It's really cute. Thank you.

1449
01:15:47,916 --> 01:15:50,166
-To a good show.
-Mmm!

1450
01:15:50,250 --> 01:15:52,708
-Mmm!
-Mmm! [laughs]

1451
01:15:53,875 --> 01:15:55,375
Uh, and Sophie,

1452
01:15:55,875 --> 01:15:58,291
me and Erin are so excited to see you.

1453
01:15:59,208 --> 01:16:01,750
And we're, uh…

1454
01:16:01,833 --> 01:16:05,541
I know. The chemistry is undeniable.

1455
01:16:05,625 --> 01:16:06,791
[chuckles]

1456
01:16:07,541 --> 01:16:09,625
At least one of us
is kissing the right person.

1457
01:16:11,416 --> 01:16:12,666
-Come here.
-[laughs]

1458
01:16:12,750 --> 01:16:14,416
[upbeat, warm music playing]

1459
01:16:14,500 --> 01:16:16,625
-[Carolyn] So cute!
-[Sophie] I know, right?

1460
01:16:27,291 --> 01:16:28,916
[Ms. Parker] Thanks, guys.

1461
01:16:29,000 --> 01:16:31,875
-[Mr. Stewart] You ready for tonight?
-[Ms. Parker] Hey, guys.

1462
01:16:31,958 --> 01:16:34,375
-[Mr. Stewart] Come in. It's time.
-[boy 1] Yeah!

1463
01:16:35,666 --> 01:16:37,750
-[girl 1] Yeah, I'm sure you did.
-[girl 2] How many?

1464
01:16:49,708 --> 01:16:51,875
-[phone alert chimes]
-[boy] All right, let's do it.

1465
01:17:00,541 --> 01:17:02,000
You can play Jenna, right?

1466
01:17:02,791 --> 01:17:04,166
And Audrey knows Dawn?

1467
01:17:04,875 --> 01:17:06,000
Excuse me?

1468
01:17:06,666 --> 01:17:09,208
I'm sorry, I have to go.
You'll be better than me anyway.

1469
01:17:12,666 --> 01:17:13,500
I'll be amazing.

1470
01:17:14,875 --> 01:17:16,083
[tires screech]

1471
01:17:16,166 --> 01:17:17,958
-Thank you, TJ.
-Love you, Soph.

1472
01:17:19,375 --> 01:17:20,750
-[door slams]
-[Sophie] Mom?

1473
01:17:28,541 --> 01:17:29,833
[sniffles]

1474
01:17:33,583 --> 01:17:35,041
I'm really scared.

1475
01:17:37,041 --> 01:17:38,166
Me too.

1476
01:17:39,208 --> 01:17:41,208
I'm so sorry, sweetheart.

1477
01:17:41,291 --> 01:17:42,458
Me too.

1478
01:17:45,791 --> 01:17:50,416
But if we're both scared,
who's gonna take care of us?

1479
01:17:51,875 --> 01:17:54,083
Your hot chauffeur husband.

1480
01:17:54,166 --> 01:17:56,000
[laughs]

1481
01:17:56,083 --> 01:17:58,750
Well, what if there is
no hot chauffeur husband?

1482
01:17:59,333 --> 01:18:01,958
Then I guess we'll have
to take care of ourselves.

1483
01:18:02,625 --> 01:18:04,166
-Women's rights.
-[laughs]

1484
01:18:06,375 --> 01:18:09,333
Wait. Shouldn't you be getting
into costume right now?

1485
01:18:09,916 --> 01:18:12,333
I don't want to miss
another minute with you.

1486
01:18:12,416 --> 01:18:13,625
[Elizabeth] Oh…

1487
01:18:14,291 --> 01:18:16,250
Oh, honey, no.

1488
01:18:16,791 --> 01:18:17,791
[sighs]

1489
01:18:19,666 --> 01:18:20,666
[sighs]

1490
01:18:20,750 --> 01:18:22,541
Your second-grade concert…

1491
01:18:22,625 --> 01:18:25,125
You cried so much. You were so proud.

1492
01:18:25,208 --> 01:18:26,375
I know.

1493
01:18:26,458 --> 01:18:28,083
No, wait. Wait. [sniffles]

1494
01:18:30,958 --> 01:18:36,500
I had looked for years
for a thing that lit me up.

1495
01:18:38,333 --> 01:18:41,166
And you found it by seven.

1496
01:18:42,333 --> 01:18:44,250
I cried because I thought,

1497
01:18:45,583 --> 01:18:47,166
no matter what,

1498
01:18:48,500 --> 01:18:53,083
you could return to that light
and you'd be okay.

1499
01:18:53,750 --> 01:18:56,208
But I don't wanna do the show without you.

1500
01:18:56,291 --> 01:18:58,291
I don't wanna do any of it without you.

1501
01:18:58,375 --> 01:19:00,708
You're never gonna be without me.

1502
01:19:04,833 --> 01:19:06,041
[sniffles]

1503
01:19:06,958 --> 01:19:10,083
I'm sorry you never found
the thing that lit you up.

1504
01:19:10,958 --> 01:19:12,666
But I did. [sniffles]

1505
01:19:17,875 --> 01:19:19,875
[band tuning up]

1506
01:19:25,083 --> 01:19:28,250
[Ted] Right here, this is us. This is us.
All the way in. All the way in. Okay,

1507
01:19:28,333 --> 01:19:31,083
-Whee! Whoo!
-[Ted sighs heavily]

1508
01:19:31,166 --> 01:19:33,166
-Whoo!
-[seat squeaking]

1509
01:19:42,083 --> 01:19:43,750
[outgoing call ringing]

1510
01:19:44,458 --> 01:19:46,041
[ringing]

1511
01:19:48,041 --> 01:19:48,916
Elizabeth?

1512
01:19:49,916 --> 01:19:51,708
You should be in Sophie's life.

1513
01:19:51,791 --> 01:19:56,958
You should be in all of their lives.
I… just need you to listen to her.

1514
01:19:57,041 --> 01:19:58,208
[gasps]

1515
01:19:59,125 --> 01:20:01,875
Uh… I will. I promise I will.

1516
01:20:02,458 --> 01:20:03,708
<i>-Okay?</i>
-[sighs]

1517
01:20:03,791 --> 01:20:06,208
<i>I love you so much, Elizabeth.</i>

1518
01:20:07,208 --> 01:20:08,916
[sobs] I love you too, Mom.

1519
01:20:10,041 --> 01:20:12,708
<i>You can tell her stories about me?</i>

1520
01:20:12,791 --> 01:20:14,541
You have all the stories.

1521
01:20:15,958 --> 01:20:18,125
<i>-I know that this is last-minute.</i>
-[mouths]

1522
01:20:18,208 --> 01:20:19,708
<i>I'm sorry, but…</i>

1523
01:20:20,416 --> 01:20:22,458
I know it would mean a lot to her
if you could

1524
01:20:22,541 --> 01:20:25,625
make it to closing night
of her show tomorrow.

1525
01:20:26,208 --> 01:20:27,333
[Linda] <i>Um…</i>

1526
01:20:27,416 --> 01:20:30,416
Is tonight okay instead?

1527
01:20:33,125 --> 01:20:34,333
[chuckles]

1528
01:20:34,916 --> 01:20:36,416
Of course, you're there already.

1529
01:20:36,500 --> 01:20:40,125
No, well, I'm sorry. Your father
said we shouldn't, but I insisted.

1530
01:20:40,208 --> 01:20:41,333
[Elizabeth chuckles]

1531
01:20:41,416 --> 01:20:42,708
-[car horn blares]
-[tires squeal]

1532
01:20:42,791 --> 01:20:46,166
-[man] Hey, hey!
-[Sophie] Oh, I'm sorry! No, no! Oh, no!

1533
01:20:46,958 --> 01:20:47,958
Oh my God.

1534
01:20:52,000 --> 01:20:53,250
[car lock bleeps]

1535
01:20:53,833 --> 01:20:55,541
-I'm so sorry, but--
-[Mallory] Don't worry.

1536
01:20:56,875 --> 01:20:57,916
I stalled.

1537
01:20:58,416 --> 01:20:59,833
I knew you'd come back.

1538
01:21:00,416 --> 01:21:03,916
And, um…
I like playing Dawn better anyway.

1539
01:21:04,000 --> 01:21:05,333
[chuckles]

1540
01:21:05,416 --> 01:21:07,666
-Are you wearing driving gloves?
-What? No.

1541
01:21:07,750 --> 01:21:09,750
[applause]

1542
01:21:16,583 --> 01:21:18,583
[girl] You're gonna do great, Sophie.

1543
01:21:20,625 --> 01:21:22,208
Hey, Sophie.

1544
01:21:22,291 --> 01:21:24,583
-I like your dress.
-Thank you.

1545
01:21:27,916 --> 01:21:29,916
[piano playing "She Used to Be Mine"]

1546
01:21:34,583 --> 01:21:37,833
<i>♪ It's not simple to say ♪</i>

1547
01:21:38,791 --> 01:21:44,666
<i>♪ That most days I don't recognize me ♪</i>

1548
01:21:44,750 --> 01:21:50,666
<i>♪ That these shoes and this apron</i>
<i>That place and its patrons ♪</i>

1549
01:21:50,750 --> 01:21:55,500
<i>♪ Have taken more than I gave them ♪</i>

1550
01:21:57,500 --> 01:22:01,000
<i>♪ It's not easy to know ♪</i>

1551
01:22:01,583 --> 01:22:06,750
<i>♪ I'm not anything like I used to be ♪</i>

1552
01:22:06,833 --> 01:22:10,708
<i>♪ Although it's true I was never ♪</i>

1553
01:22:10,791 --> 01:22:13,833
<i>♪ Attention's sweet center ♪</i>

1554
01:22:13,916 --> 01:22:17,875
<i>♪ I still remember that girl ♪</i>

1555
01:22:19,000 --> 01:22:23,791
<i>♪ She's imperfect, but she tries ♪</i>

1556
01:22:24,500 --> 01:22:29,500
<i>♪ She is good, but she lies ♪</i>

1557
01:22:30,375 --> 01:22:35,000
<i>♪ She is hard on herself ♪</i>

1558
01:22:36,041 --> 01:22:40,500
<i>♪ She is broken and won't ask for help ♪</i>

1559
01:22:42,083 --> 01:22:46,875
<i>♪ She is messy, but she's kind ♪</i>

1560
01:22:47,791 --> 01:22:53,625
<i>♪ She is lonely most of the time ♪</i>

1561
01:22:53,708 --> 01:22:56,583
<i>♪ She is all of this mixed up ♪</i>

1562
01:22:56,666 --> 01:23:01,041
<i>♪ And baked in a beautiful pie ♪</i>

1563
01:23:02,166 --> 01:23:05,750
<i>♪ She is gone, but she used to be ♪</i>

1564
01:23:05,833 --> 01:23:10,000
<i>♪ Mine ♪</i>

1565
01:23:12,541 --> 01:23:16,166
<i>♪ It's not what I asked for ♪</i>

1566
01:23:16,250 --> 01:23:18,875
<i>♪ Sometimes life ♪</i>

1567
01:23:19,583 --> 01:23:22,833
<i>♪ Just slips in through a back door ♪</i>

1568
01:23:22,916 --> 01:23:25,750
<i>♪ And carves out a person ♪</i>

1569
01:23:25,833 --> 01:23:30,000
<i>♪ And makes you believe it's all true ♪</i>

1570
01:23:31,500 --> 01:23:34,000
<i>♪ And now I've got you ♪</i>

1571
01:23:35,375 --> 01:23:38,750
<i>♪ You're not what I asked for ♪</i>

1572
01:23:39,416 --> 01:23:45,041
<i>♪ If I'm honest</i>
<i>I know I would give it all back ♪</i>

1573
01:23:45,125 --> 01:23:48,208
<i>♪ For a chance to start over ♪</i>

1574
01:23:48,791 --> 01:23:53,333
<i>♪ And rewrite an ending or two ♪</i>

1575
01:23:53,916 --> 01:23:56,791
<i>♪ For that girl that I knew ♪</i>

1576
01:23:56,875 --> 01:24:01,375
<i>♪ Who was reckless just enough ♪</i>

1577
01:24:02,375 --> 01:24:04,250
<i>♪ Who gets hurt ♪</i>

1578
01:24:05,416 --> 01:24:08,291
<i>♪ But who learns how to toughen up ♪</i>

1579
01:24:08,375 --> 01:24:11,041
<i>♪ When she's bruised ♪</i>

1580
01:24:11,125 --> 01:24:16,875
<i>♪ And gets used by a man who can't love ♪</i>

1581
01:24:17,500 --> 01:24:23,166
<i>♪ And then she'll get stuck</i>
<i>And be scared ♪</i>

1582
01:24:23,250 --> 01:24:28,666
<i>♪ Of the life that's inside her</i>
<i>Growing stronger each day ♪</i>

1583
01:24:29,166 --> 01:24:34,416
<i>♪ Till it finally reminds her</i>
<i>To fight just a little ♪</i>

1584
01:24:35,000 --> 01:24:39,791
<i>♪ To bring back the fire in her eyes ♪</i>

1585
01:24:39,875 --> 01:24:44,041
<i>♪ That's been gone but used to be ♪</i>

1586
01:24:44,125 --> 01:24:50,625
<i>♪ Mine ♪</i>

1587
01:24:52,875 --> 01:24:55,000
<i>♪ Oh, used to be ♪</i>

1588
01:24:55,750 --> 01:25:02,750
<i>♪ Mine ♪</i>

1589
01:25:06,416 --> 01:25:08,041
<i>♪ She is messy ♪</i>

1590
01:25:08,916 --> 01:25:10,958
<i>♪ But she's kind ♪</i>

1591
01:25:11,958 --> 01:25:17,666
<i>♪ She is lonely most of the time ♪</i>

1592
01:25:17,750 --> 01:25:21,125
<i>♪ She is all of this mixed up ♪</i>

1593
01:25:21,208 --> 01:25:24,416
<i>♪ And baked in a beautiful pie ♪</i>

1594
01:25:29,125 --> 01:25:31,250
<i>♪ She is gone ♪</i>

1595
01:25:32,416 --> 01:25:35,541
<i>♪ But she used to be ♪</i>

1596
01:25:37,125 --> 01:25:43,541
<i>♪ Mine ♪</i>

1597
01:25:45,833 --> 01:25:48,041
[clapping]

1598
01:25:53,791 --> 01:25:55,791
[crickets chirping]

1599
01:25:59,083 --> 01:26:01,083
[crickets continue chirping]

1600
01:26:03,375 --> 01:26:05,583
["Silver Springs"
by Fleetwood Mac playing]

1601
01:26:24,208 --> 01:26:28,750
<i>♪ You could be my silver spring ♪</i>

1602
01:26:29,791 --> 01:26:33,875
<i>♪ Blue green, colors flashin' ♪</i>

1603
01:26:34,791 --> 01:26:38,875
<i>♪ I would be your only dream ♪</i>

1604
01:26:39,500 --> 01:26:42,083
<i>♪ Your shinin' autumn ♪</i>

1605
01:26:42,166 --> 01:26:46,791
<i>♪ Ocean crashin' ♪</i>

1606
01:26:48,250 --> 01:26:52,416
<i>♪ And don't say that she's pretty ♪</i>

1607
01:26:53,500 --> 01:26:57,791
<i>♪ And did you say that she loved you ♪</i>

1608
01:26:58,958 --> 01:27:03,041
<i>♪ Baby, I don't wanna know ♪</i>

1609
01:27:12,208 --> 01:27:16,458
<i>♪ So I'll begin not to love you ♪</i>

1610
01:27:18,041 --> 01:27:22,666
<i>♪ Turn around, see me runnin' ♪</i>

1611
01:27:22,750 --> 01:27:27,000
<i>♪ I'll say I loved you years ago ♪</i>

1612
01:27:28,166 --> 01:27:33,125
<i>♪ Tell myself you never loved me ♪</i>

1613
01:27:33,625 --> 01:27:35,208
<i>♪ No ♪</i>

1614
01:27:36,666 --> 01:27:40,791
<i>♪ And don't say that she's pretty ♪</i>

1615
01:27:42,166 --> 01:27:46,375
<i>♪ And did you say that she loved you ♪</i>

1616
01:27:47,583 --> 01:27:51,541
<i>♪ Baby, I don't wanna know ♪</i>

1617
01:27:54,791 --> 01:27:57,375
<i>♪ Oh, no ♪</i>

